                        "form": "магистра́лях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9ee27d1-a98b-387a-ab10-8239452bb357",
                        "entry_id": "6b603686-9da5-3022-9711-afde60f2ef6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "основная линия, главное направление в какой-либо сети или инфраструктуре"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "792c9946-9486-42b7-8794-04133e567f1f",
                                "sense_id": "c9ee27d1-a98b-387a-ab10-8239452bb357",
                                "text": "Вот и станция Тайга, откуда идёт ветка на Томск. .. я навлёк на себя .. гнев томских газет за то, что провёл магистраль не через Томск, ограничившись веткой к нему."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "608be4af-87da-4f44-9aef-8ce73e424d43",
                                "sense_id": "c9ee27d1-a98b-387a-ab10-8239452bb357",
                                "text": ".. Наде было уже знакомо много станций, и хотя из окна вагона, но она уже видела раньше и не один раз многие города по магистрали Петербург — Севастополь, и с каждым у неё уже было связано кое-что."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54b304c8-41e5-379f-98a0-56bdca4032c0",
                        "entry_id": "6b603686-9da5-3022-9711-afde60f2ef6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. основное направление в развитии чего-либо, в каком-либо процессе"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "017a6a88-aa88-40fe-a43d-01304930276e",
                        "source_entry_id": "6b603686-9da5-3022-9711-afde60f2ef6d",
                        "target_lang_word": "main line",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "main line",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3778074-8959-36a9-83bd-9950877def0d",
                                        "entry_id": "565f7661-5842-3a48-a169-04cffa8aaee5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A standard sequence of opening moves considered to be best play."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aeb762dc-89da-45b8-9bdf-d502ef912c88",
                                                "sense_id": "c3778074-8959-36a9-83bd-9950877def0d",
                                                "text": "In that game, Carlsen sidestepped the main line of the Berlin Defense with 4 d4, hoping to unsettle Karjakin. That did not work, and chances were equal for most of the game."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9293af42-1e83-42e4-90b2-ea77d738773a",
                                                "sense_id": "c3778074-8959-36a9-83bd-9950877def0d",
                                                "text": "8.Qd2 is the old main line of the Poisoned Pawn from the days of Fischer and Kasparov."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fe2b9d7-1113-4a17-a521-5a74bf37ff08",
                                                "sense_id": "c3778074-8959-36a9-83bd-9950877def0d",
                                                "text": "Adams, the No1 seed in the Isle of Man, has always favoured 3 Nd2 against the French and, when his Polish opponent, below, followed a main line, Adams was very willing to go along."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6310654-533f-3633-b321-a0bc64449cd3",
                                        "entry_id": "565f7661-5842-3a48-a169-04cffa8aaee5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of mainline."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32cb7f7c-18ac-4c0d-9811-b2b55e16ce2c",
                                                "sense_id": "c6310654-533f-3633-b321-a0bc64449cd3",
                                                "text": "Gavin Johns, chairman of the Swanage Railway Trust, said: \"I would like to thank our stakeholders for their far-sighted investment of £5.5 million to re-connect Swanage and Corfe Castle with the main line, which included £1.8m from the Government's coastal communities fund, so we could restore our 1950s heritage diesel trains for running on the main line.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "main line",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8e55dd4-0f65-3f6e-9bc5-759e81679a5b",
                                        "entry_id": "35ac1867-7a8a-33bf-9a67-aa863e343fc4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of mainline."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c48f88b-02ad-452a-ba13-9b15d32c8a8e",
                                                "sense_id": "d8e55dd4-0f65-3f6e-9bc5-759e81679a5b",
                                                "text": "Caruana chose the Petroff 2 Nf3 Nf6, which used to be the weapon of choice for players aiming for a half point as Black, was relegated for some years due to the popularity of the Berlin 1 e4 e5 2 Nf3 Nc6 3 Bb5 Nf6, but has returned to favour as the main line Berlin with an early queen swap has been outmoded by 4 d3."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2632ef6a-8a6f-4182-b41f-458780b0995e",
                        "source_entry_id": "6b603686-9da5-3022-9711-afde60f2ef6d",
                        "target_lang_word": "thoroughfare",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thoroughfare",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "461ac537-3440-3650-98ff-6e4dee1d0505",
                                        "entry_id": "2dc42725-6563-3481-b83e-28e03b3fc374",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A passage; a way through."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85548f13-aac6-4c03-b727-8e82c234d7fc",
                                                "sense_id": "461ac537-3440-3650-98ff-6e4dee1d0505",
                                                "text": "“I ask you,” cried Lloyd George in 1909. “Are we to have all the ways of reform, financial and social, blocked simply by a notice board: ‘No thoroughfare. By order of Nathanial Rothschild’?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3e16624-eadf-41cc-b64c-c21f09c811d2",
                                                "sense_id": "461ac537-3440-3650-98ff-6e4dee1d0505",
                                                "text": "In the scullery Smiley had once more checked his thoroughfare, shoved some deck-chairs aside, and pinned a string to the mangle to guide him because he saw badly in the dark."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                        "entry_id": "2dc42725-6563-3481-b83e-28e03b3fc374",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A road open at both ends or connecting one area with another; a highway or main street."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6237927-c028-49c4-ac4e-d9e708155b09",
                                                "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                                "text": "a dozen houses were quickly blazing, including those of Sir John Fielding and two other justices, and four in Holborn – one of the greatest thoroughfares in London – which were all burning at the same time, and burned until they went out of themselves, for the people cut the engine hose, and would not suffer the firemen to play upon the flames."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2cfc3db-79a8-4383-81d4-d702c0dbfeb5",
                                                "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                                "text": "With some of it on the south and more of it on the north of the great main thoroughfare that connects Aldgate and the East India Docks, St. Bede's at this period of its history was perhaps the poorest and most miserable parish in the East End of London."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e558a47e-e660-4714-8b79-e606ddb53d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                                "text": "East [Street] and West Street form a single thoroughfare running as a backbone through the village, flanked by neat, painted cottages of predominantly 18th-century brick."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c575266-48a8-43ad-868e-92cd7c545913",
                                                "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                                "text": "Local art is now a viable industry, and hundreds of islanders make a living in it. The thoroughfare of Oneroa village is lined with shops and galleries full of their work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e8e1bc3-4883-4819-b8d4-98a479c43b66",
                                                "sense_id": "1b578cce-d887-3092-90f1-c8bf49f075d8",
                                                "text": "Mr. Roscoe, on the contrary, has claimed none of the accorded privileges of talent. He has shut himself up in no garden of thought, no elysium of fancy; but has gone forth into the highways and thoroughfares of life; […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f98fb01d-6151-37da-9b76-d500ee4877f3",
                                        "entry_id": "2dc42725-6563-3481-b83e-28e03b3fc374",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of going through; passage; travel, transit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96b2a832-a942-4cfd-a6b8-b77e2f3c2554",
                                                "sense_id": "f98fb01d-6151-37da-9b76-d500ee4877f3",
                                                "text": "The sign leading to the other carriage reads: No thoroughfare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2370b66-b348-47d4-8bc5-57b9ac273202",
                                                "sense_id": "f98fb01d-6151-37da-9b76-d500ee4877f3",
                                                "text": "and made one realm, / Hell and this world, one realm, one continent / Of easy thorough-fare."
                                            }
                                        ]
